#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:1
msgid "Release 2.23.0 (2024-06-03)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:3
msgid ""
"New builtin: `builtins.warn` [\\#306026](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"issues/306026) [\\#10592](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10592)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:5
msgid ""
"`builtins.warn` behaves like `builtins.trace \"warning: ${msg}\"`, has an "
"accurate log level, and is controlled by the options [`debugger-on-trace`]"
"(../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-debugger-on-trace), [`debugger-on-warn`]"
"(../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-debugger-on-warn) and [`abort-on-warn`](../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-abort-on-warn)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:10
msgid "Make `nix build --keep-going` consistent with `nix-build --keep-going`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:12
msgid ""
"This means that if e.g. multiple fixed-output derivations fail to build, all "
"hash mismatches are displayed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:15
msgid ""
"Modify `nix derivation {add,show}` JSON format [\\#9866](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/issues/9866) [\\#10722](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10722)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:17
msgid ""
"The JSON format for derivations has been slightly revised to better conform "
"to our [data modeling guidelines](../development/data-modeling.md). In "
"particular, the hash algorithm and content addressing method of content-"
"addressed derivation outputs are now separated into two fields `hashAlgo` "
"and `method`, rather than one field with an arcane `:`\\-separated format."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:21
msgid ""
"This JSON format is only used by the experimental `nix derivation` family of "
"commands, at this time. Future revisions are expected as the JSON format is "
"still not entirely in compliance even after these changes."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:24
msgid ""
"Warn on unknown settings anywhere in the command line [\\#10701](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10701)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:26
msgid ""
"All `nix` commands will now properly warn when an unknown option is "
"specified anywhere in the command line."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:28 source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:63
msgid "Before:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:38 source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:69
msgid "After:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:50
msgid ""
"`nix env shell` is the new `nix shell`, and `nix shell` remains an accepted "
"alias [\\#10504](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/10504) [\\#10807]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10807)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:52
msgid ""
"This is part of an effort to bring more structure to the CLI subcommands."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:54
msgid ""
"`nix env` will be about the process environment. Future commands may include "
"`nix env run` and `nix env print-env`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:57
msgid ""
"It is also somewhat analogous to the [planned](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"issues/10504) `nix dev shell` (currently `nix develop`), which is less about "
"environment variables, and more about running a development shell, which is "
"a more powerful command, but also requires more setup."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:59
msgid ""
"Flake operations that expect derivations now print the failing value and its "
"type [\\#10778](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10778)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:61
msgid ""
"In errors like `flake output attribute 'nixosConfigurations.yuki.config' is "
"not a derivation or path`, the message now includes the failing value and "
"type."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:75
msgid ""
"`fetchTree` now fetches Git repositories shallowly by default [\\#10028]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10028)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:77
msgid ""
"`builtins.fetchTree` now clones Git repositories shallowly by default, which "
"reduces network traffic and disk usage significantly in many cases."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:79
msgid ""
"Previously, the default behavior was to clone the full history of a specific "
"tag or branch (e.g. `ref`) and only afterwards extract the files of one "
"specific revision."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:81
msgid ""
"From now on, the `ref` and `allRefs` arguments will be ignored, except if "
"shallow cloning is disabled by setting `shallow = false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:83
msgid ""
"The defaults for `builtins.fetchGit` remain unchanged. Here, shallow cloning "
"has to be enabled manually by passing `shallow = true`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:85
msgid ""
"Store object info JSON format now uses `null` rather than omitting fields "
"[\\#9995](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9995)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:87
msgid ""
"The [store object info JSON format](../protocols/json/store-object-info.md), "
"used for e.g. `nix path-info`, no longer omits fields to indicate absent "
"information, but instead includes the fields with a `null` value. For "
"example, `\"ca\": null` is used to indicate a store object that isn't "
"content-addressed rather than omitting the `ca` field entirely. This makes "
"records of this sort more self-describing, and easier to consume "
"programmatically."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:91
msgid ""
"We will follow this design principle going forward; the [data modeling "
"guidelines](../development/data-modeling.md) in the contributing section "
"have been updated accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:94
msgid "Large path warnings [\\#10661](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10661)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:96
msgid ""
"Nix can now warn when evaluation of a Nix expression causes a large path to "
"be copied to the Nix store. The threshold for this warning can be configured "
"using [the `warn-large-path-threshold` setting](../command-ref/conf-file."
"md#conf-warn-large-path-threshold), e.g. `--warn-large-path-threshold 100M` "
"will warn about paths larger than 100 MiB."
msgstr ""
